# 1. PRIMARY OBJECTIVE

Develop a functional bookmark import system that allows the owner to upload browser-exported Netscape HTML bookmark files and import them into the existing Neon PostgreSQL database.

The system must:

1. Accept browser bookmark HTML files.
2. Support selecting multiple HTML files.
3. Parse bookmarks and nested source folders.
4. Extract and preserve original bookmark information.
5. Identify duplicates using normalized FULL URLs.
6. Preserve different URLs from the same domain.
7. Preview results before importing.
8. Allow the owner to select a destination category.
9. Respect existing manual category assignments.
10. Save imported bookmarks in Neon PostgreSQL.
11. Preserve import occurrences and original folder paths.
12. Display import results and basic import history.
13. Prevent duplicate canonical bookmarks during repeated imports.

Do not implement AI classification, full export/backup functionality, or advanced metadata enrichment in this phase.

