## Missing Titles

A bookmark with an empty title is still valid if its URL is valid.

For example:

```html
<A HREF="https://example.com"></A>
```

The application should:

- Keep the original title as an empty string in source occurrence metadata.
- Generate a readable display fallback from the hostname or URL path.
- Allow the owner to edit the title later.

Do not discard valid bookmarks because they have missing titles.

# 5. ABSOLUTE RULE — FULL-URL DUPLICATE DETECTION

This is the most important requirement.

**Never use hostname-only or domain-only duplicate detection.**

A bookmark's identity depends on its conservatively normalized full URL.

Examples:

| URL A | URL B | Result |
|---|---|---|
| `https://youtube.com` | `https://youtube.com/` | Duplicate |
| `https://youtube.com/` | `https://youtube.com/watch?v=123` | Different |
| `https://youtube.com/watch?v=123` | `https://youtube.com/watch?v=456` | Different |
| `https://github.com/user/repo1` | `https://github.com/user/repo2` | Different |
| `https://example.com/page?id=1` | `https://example.com/page?id=2` | Different |
| `https://example.com/a` | `https://example.com/a/` | Different by default |
| `https://example.com/p#one` | `https://example.com/p#two` | Different by default |

## Normalization Requirements

Reuse the approved Phase 1 URL normalization implementation.

Allow conservative normalization such as:

- Trimming surrounding whitespace.
- Standard hostname and scheme case normalization.
- Empty root path and `/` equivalence.
- Equivalent default-port handling.

Never automatically:

- Strip query parameters.
- Strip UTM parameters.
- Sort query parameters.
- Remove fragments.
- Ignore non-root trailing slashes.
- Convert HTTP to HTTPS.
- Merge `www` and non-`www` hostnames.
- Merge different URL paths.
- Collapse redirect destinations.

Original URLs must be preserved independently of their identity keys.

If Phase 1 normalization violates these requirements, correct it without changing unrelated code.

Use the existing database uniqueness constraint for owner-scoped URL identity.

The database constraint, not a client-side duplicate check, must prevent concurrent canonical duplicates.

# 6. DUPLICATE RECONCILIATION

Implement duplicate reconciliation against:

1. Other entries in the same uploaded file.
2. Entries in other files in the current upload.
3. Canonical bookmarks already stored in Neon.

Example:

First imported HTML:

```text
https://github.com/user/repo
https://youtube.com/watch?v=abc
```

Second imported HTML:

```text
https://github.com/user/repo
https://youtube.com/watch?v=xyz
```

Result:

- Existing GitHub URL: duplicate canonical identity.
- Existing YouTube video ABC: retained.
- New YouTube video XYZ: inserted.
- Both files' source occurrences: preserved.

The final canonical library has three bookmarks, not four.

### Duplicate Handling Rules

When a duplicate full URL is detected:

- Do not insert another canonical bookmark.
- Link the imported occurrence to the existing bookmark.
- Preserve the incoming original title and folder path in occurrence history.
- Preserve the existing bookmark's user-edited title.
- Preserve its notes and favorite status.
- Preserve its manually selected category.
- Preserve category locks.
- Never silently overwrite user changes.

A repeated file import must not increase the canonical bookmark count.

However, an explicitly repeated import may have its own import-history record and source occurrences.

Use an idempotency key per commit operation and occurrence indexes to prevent accidental duplication caused by retries.

Do not use the source file checksum alone to discard all future import history.

