Revalidate the file or trusted staged content before committing.

Expired or stale previews must require a new preview.

# 10. CATEGORY CONFLICT RESOLUTION

Consider this scenario:

An existing bookmark:

`https://youtube.com/watch?v=react123`

Current category:

`Development / Tutorials`

The owner previously selected that category manually.

A new HTML file contains the same full URL under:

`Entertainment / Videos`

Do not move it automatically.

### Default Conflict Behavior

**Keep existing category.**

For the basic UI, provide these options where supported:

1. Keep Existing Category — default.
2. Move to Selected Category — only after explicit owner confirmation.
3. Add Secondary Folder Reference — only if supported by the existing placement model.

If secondary placements are not implemented yet, do not simulate them by cloning a canonical bookmark.

When the owner selected a global import destination category, apply it automatically only to genuinely new bookmarks.

Existing canonical bookmarks require explicit conflict resolution before changing categories.

A manual category lock cannot be overwritten by import heuristics or source-folder matching.

